#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162105 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "277b8807-fb74-5ad3-a89b-92dbf90bc075" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Conditional Probability Mass Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d146954b-107a-5bf5-b2c2-58b2d76d2f0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363317} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce85799-ee97-543b-b79a-08bcfeb894e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363318} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d3ebc3-d64d-5e87-9163-151fc4e5359e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363319} {:answer/id #uuid "cf3c3657-5609-567b-9359-aff272cdd30d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363320} {:answer/id #uuid "4676d494-1558-5c75-a0ac-1ffbf28c079b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4676d494-1558-5c75-a0ac-1ffbf28c079b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363321} :answer-field/id #uuid "d59b5ddd-f1f5-574e-9fb1-16006eceeb0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13d8d8db-94c8-50ea-a54d-7920bc95617e" :question/math-academy-id "q-142902" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{5}{27}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{8}{27}$ | $\\frac{2}{27}$ |\n\nCompute ${f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,1)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,1)=P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=1).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=4\\,|\\,Y=1)=\\frac{P(X=4,Y=1)}{P(Y=1)}=\\frac{f(4,1)}{{f}_{Y}(1)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(1) & =f(2,1)+f(4,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{27}+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(4,1)=\\frac{1}{9}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{Y}(1)=\\frac{8}{27}$ and $f(4,1)=\\frac{1}{9}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(4\\,|\\,1) & =P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4,1)}{{f}_{Y}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{9})}{(\\frac{8}{27})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "348dfcb8-2325-5929-b622-5423b7e37a53" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability Over an Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dcc4c86-8874-58a9-ac30-b8fea76a7d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159465} {:answer/id #uuid "9e3d5dc9-0fd4-5e6b-94c2-978465a52970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value